            {"q": "What did the first human trial show, according to the passage?", "a": ["That penicillin was too weak to help people", "That the drug worked only on scratches", "That penicillin was dangerous in large doses", "That the drug worked, and the real problem was making enough"], "c": 3, "kind": "gist"},
            {"q": "Where was a highly productive strain of the mould found?", "a": ["In Fleming’s London laboratory", "In the soil of an Oxford garden", "On a mouldy melon from a market in Illinois", "On bread in an army kitchen"], "c": 2, "kind": "detail"},
            {"q": "Which statement best sums up the passage?", "a": ["Fleming found penicillin by chance and, working alone for a decade, made it into a drug for the war", "A chance observation became a mass-produced drug only through the later work of the Oxford team and American industry", "The Oxford team found penicillin first, and Fleming’s later paper took the credit and the Nobel Prize", "Drug companies made penicillin during the war, and the laboratory scientists had little to do with it"], "c": 1, "kind": "gist"},
